this is believed to be the now missing  tourist boat leaving the marina for a  sightseeing trip  but the waters surrounding the  picturesque saratoco peninsula are now a  scene of tragedy  the boat had sent a distress signal to  the coast guard just after one yesterday  afternoon saying they had taken on water  and were beginning to tilt  two hours later they lost contact  26 people including two children were on  board  a mammoth rescue effort with patrol  boats helicopters and divers is ongoing  so far the bodies of ten people  seven men and three women have been  recovered  today a disaster prevention helicopter  in hokkaido will also participate in the  search activity  in cooperation with the japanese coast  guard the self-defense forces and the  police we will do our utmost to rescue  people whose safety is unknown  it's reported everyone on board was  wearing a life jacket sea conditions had  been rough with waves up to two meters  high  prime minister says searches will  continue until everyone is accounted for  relevant organizations will continue to  do their utmost in search and rescue  activities with the highest priority on  saving lives  the government's transport ministry is  looking into the operators safety  standards this is their third incident  in two years  the latest is now under investigation  whilst emergency services continue to  search for any sign of survival  ashton harinag sky news
 

